    <!--
      Run every test with the project-level Test action (Alt+F6) and with "ant test".

      Two separate things were wrong.

      1. build-impl.xml hardcodes testincludes="**/*Test.java" in -do-test-run.  Every test class here
         is named test<Something>.java - prefix, not suffix - so that pattern matched nothing, TestNG
         was handed no classes at all, and it responded by printing its usage and failing.

      2. Only one MarklinControlStation can exist per JVM.  NetworkProxy binds a fixed UDP port
         (15730) and neither it nor MarklinControlStation exposes any way to close it, so the station
         built by the first test class holds that port until the JVM exits, and every later class
         fails to start one.  Running all classes in a single TestNG process cannot work, however the
         includes are written - which is why the run kept dying a few seconds in, having completed one
         class, with an empty results directory.

      So each class is run as its own invocation below.  The TestNG Ant task forks a JVM per
      invocation, which gives every class the clean process it needs - the same isolation it gets when
      run as a single test file from the IDE.  They run one after another, and -post-test-run still
      fails the build at the end if any of them failed.

      Running a single test file from the IDE is unaffected: that goes through -do-test-run-single.

      Not in the list: testAutoDetect, which probes the network for a real Central Station at a
      hardcoded address.  It is an integration test against hardware and cannot pass unless the layout
      is connected.

      Adding a test class means adding a line here.  That is the price of the per-class isolation; the
      alternative is a shutdown path on MarklinControlStation that releases the socket, which would
      let the whole suite share one JVM and make this list unnecessary.
    -->
    <target depends="init,compile-test,-init-test-run-module-properties,-pre-test-run" if="have.tests" name="-do-test-run">
        <!-- The tests live in test/core, test/ui, test/regression and test/support since 2026-08-22 -
             see test/README.md for which folder a new one belongs in.  These entries do not name the
             folder, because testincludes below is a FILE pattern and **/ already spans it. -->
        <macrodef name="test-one-class">
            <attribute name="class"/>
            <sequential>
                <echo message="---------- @{class} ----------"/>
                <j2seproject3:test includes="${includes}" testincludes="**/@{class}.java"/>
            </sequential>
        </macrodef>

